# SPA fallback for the app's client-side routes.
#
# Listed explicitly rather than with /app/*, which cannot work here. Two traps,
# both found with wrangler's local Pages emulator:
#
#   /app/*  /app/index.html  200
#     Silently discarded. Pages canonicalises /app/index.html back to /app/,
#     re-matching the pattern, so it detects an infinite loop and drops the
#     rule. wrangler warns; the deployed site says nothing and serves the
#     landing page for every route in the app.
#
#   /app/*  /app-shell  200
#     Parses cleanly and is far worse. Cloudflare evaluates _redirects BEFORE
#     static assets -- the reverse of Netlify -- so a catch-all rewrites every
#     script, the stylesheet, the manifest and the service worker to HTML, and
#     the app never boots.
#
# These prefixes are safe because no built asset lives under them: the app's
# files are in /app/assets, /app/icons, /app/screenshots and /app/video.
#
# ADD A LINE HERE WHEN YOU ADD A ROUTE to App.tsx. Anything missed still loads
# via dist/app/404.html, but with a 404 status instead of 200.
#
# The target is /app-shell -- no extension, outside /app/ -- because Pages
# strips .html and canonicalises /x/index.html to /x/, either of which puts the
# destination back inside the pattern and recreates the loop above.
/app/login           /app-shell   200
/app/privacy         /app-shell   200
/app/about           /app-shell   200
/app/group-setup     /app-shell   200
/app/settings        /app-shell   200
/app/settings/*      /app-shell   200
/app/join/*          /app-shell   200
/app/lists/*         /app-shell   200
